    "stdout_tail": "{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"api_error_status\":null,\"duration_ms\":268703,\"duration_api_ms\":180159,\"ttft_ms\":2751,\"ttft_stream_ms\":1911,\"time_to_request_ms\":89,\"num_turns\":25,\"result\":\"All tests pass. Here's a summary of the change:\\n\\n---\\n\\n**What changed:** `BranchesFor` in `internal/cli/export.go` (line 1478).\\n\\nThe method determines which branch a session is grouped under during export. Previously, it checked the session's metadata branch first \u2014 so a session recorded on `feature-x` would always land in the `feature-x` folder, even after `feature-x` was merged into `main` and the checkpoint became reachable from the default branch.\\n\\nThe fix reverses the priority: default-branch reachability is checked **first**. If the checkpoint's ID appears in `DefaultCheckpointIDs` (built by walking the default branch's git log), the session is grouped under the default branch. The `SourceBranch` field is set before `BranchesFor` is called, so the original feature-branch name is still preserved in the output.\\n\\n**Validation commands that passed:**\\n- `go test ./internal/cli/ -run \\\"TestSnapshotMetadata|TestExportSelectsLatest|TestBuildBranchDirectories|TestExportDefault|TestExportUses\\\" -v -count=1`\\n- `go test ./internal/cli/ -run \\\"^Test\\\" -count=1`\",\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"session_id\":\"5b467352-34b0-477c-94fc-9e43fa5bcf45\",\"total_cost_usd\":1.0410501,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":27,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":68225,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":1630897,\"output_tokens\":9490,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":68225,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\",\"iterations\":[{\"input_tokens\":1,\"output_tokens\":292,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":84645,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":160,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_i